<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kremsmünster Abbey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">777</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kremsmünster Abbey is a Benedictine monastery in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-austria">Upper Austria</a>, founded in 777 by Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tassilo-iii-of-bavaria">Tassilo III of Bavaria</a> to spread <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> and settlement on the eastern frontier. Its treasury holds the Tassilo Chalice, a gilded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> chalice given by Tassilo and his wife Liutpirga. Rebuilt in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baroque">Baroque</a> style, the abbey still houses a community of monks and a well-known school.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kremsmunster-abbey.jpg" alt="Kremsmünster Abbey" width="320" height="182" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: C.Stadler/Bwag · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kremsm%C3%BCnster_-_Stift.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
